From 7475f1eecbe3066b92c566a8c12fbbf799f67d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 10:40:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02547/11362] [outer-loop] M2-v2: per-object
 (connected-component) translate -- the color-aware object segmenter

Routes the operator's 'color-aware object segmenter' build INTO the EXISTING M2-v2
ObjectDeltaModel (arc_world_model_dsl.py) rather than a parallel module -- my four ARC
bridge probes empirically re-derived and VALIDATED M2-v2's object-level thesis, so the
right move is to extend it. (Avoids the parallel-edifice the operator warned against.)

THE GAP (measured, not assumed): M2-v2's existing "translate" rule is per-COLOR-GLOBAL
(s==color moves ALL cells of a color), so it induces ALL-NOOP whenever a movable object
shares its colour with a static object (goal/wall). Direct measurement: cn04 induced
all-noop (held-out dynamics_accuracy 0.000) despite the object-centric probe finding cn04
has 50 clean single-object translations.

THE FIX (additive, backward-compatible): _color_components (4-connected per-colour
components = objects) + _detect_object_translation (one component translated rigidly while
other same-colour objects stayed) + a new ("translate_obj", color, shape_sig, dy, dx) rule
that moves only the component(s) matching the learned object's position-invariant shape (so
it generalizes to an unseen position). Selection maximizes dynamics accuracy, tie-breaking
toward the SIMPLER per-colour rule so single-object games are unchanged.

ISOLATED RESULT (baseline=per-object-disabled vs extended, M2's own dynamics_accuracy):
  cn04: 0.000 -> 0.174 (+0.174)   ka59: 0.001 -> 0.151 (+0.149)
  sp80/ar25/tu93: +0.000 (per-colour translate already fit; unchanged -- back-compat)
The lift lands exactly on the games where per-colour-global was all-noop, as predicted.
Deltas are modest because these games also have HUD/selection-highlight changes a move rule
alone does not reproduce (so EXACT whole-grid match stays ~0; partial dynamics accuracy is
the honest metric). Per-object translate is necessary, not sufficient.

V1 limitation (documented): shape-based object identity cannot disambiguate a movable object
from a static one of IDENTICAL shape. Tests: 6/6 pass (4 back-compat + 2 new, assert-bearing
per CLAUDE.md); consumer arc_execution_guided_world_model imports clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
